Z||000000||mdjoneses||08-13-2000||02:21 PM||||I'm having trouble getting my car started. It's coming out of a 10 year storage. I drained the gas and put Mobile high-test in with some H2o remover +fuel injector cleaner. Has fresh oil/filter. New spark<BR>plugs/wires /dist-cap/rotor. We put some oil down each plug hole and primed the engine with A oil pump primer. We turned it over with the plugs out. It turned over ez. But once we had it all back together it only runs for a second or two.  fuel pump is working. We bleed off some air from the shrouder valve. When we shoot some starter fluid into throttle  body it runs longer. The car sounds normal when it turns over and starts but stalls soon after. Any ideas on why it wont run?<BR>86se/V6/2.8    thanx  Mark<BR> <BR> <BR>||||reg||9
